<script type="text/javascript">
    
	$(document).ready(function () {
		var logConsole = function (str) {
			console.log(str);
		};
		if ($('#tabPortlet_228189 .divTabEdit').val() == "True") {
			var isModern = ('True');
			if (isModern.toLowerCase() == "true") {
				var tabObj = $('#tabPortlet_228189 ');
				var tabM = $('#ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl26_divTabs').attr('portlet') == 'tab';

				function activate() {
					$(tabObj).scrollingTabs({
						tabs: [{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl26_divTabs_0","title":"November 17, 2026 - Notice of Proposed Rule Development Workshop School Board Policy","content":"<p>The School Board of Polk County, Florida (“<strong>Board</strong>”) will hold a public workshop on the following revised Board policies <strong>Policy 1120, Policy 1130, Policy 1211, Policy 3120, Policy 3130, Policy 3211, Policy 3220, Policy 4120, Policy 4130, Policy 4211, Policy 6520, Policy 7217, Policy 7310, Policy 8330, Policy 8405, Policy 8407, Policy 8470, Policy 8475, Policy 9120, Policy 9211 and Policy 9215</strong>, on <strong>November 17, 2026</strong> at the Jim Miles Professional Development Center, located at 4270 Wallace Road, Lakeland, FL 33812. The proposed changes to the above referenced Board policies will be published on the Polk County Public Schools (“<strong>PCPS</strong>”) website as part of the meeting agenda seven days prior to the meeting. Meeting agendas can be accessed at:</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/about/meetings\" title=\"Link to PCPS Meeting webpage\">https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/about/meetings</a></p>\n<p>The proposed changes may be requested prior to the meeting agenda publication by emailing the Public Records Office at <a href=\"mailto:teresa.griffin@polk-fl.net\">teresa.griffin@polk-fl.net</a>. Copies may be obtained at the Polk County Public Schools Administrative Offices between the hours of 8:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. in the Public Records Office.<br>\n<br>\nThe revised Board policies will be placed on the Board’s agenda for a public hearing during the <strong>January 26, 2027</strong> meeting at the Polk County Public Schools Administrative Offices, located at 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830.<br>\n<br>\nWritten comments may be submitted within 21 days of the date of this notice to Legal Services, 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830. Substantially affected persons may, within 14 days of the date of this notice, file an objection to this rulemaking with the Board. The objection shall specify the portions of the proposed rules to which the person objects and the specific reasons for the objections.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 1120 Employment of Administrators</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.&nbsp;<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1001.10, F.S. 1012.01, F.S. 1012.23, F.S. 1012.315, F.S. 1012.32, F.S. 1012.33, F.S. 1012.55, F.S. 1012.56, 42 U.S.C. 9858f, F.S. 1012.22</p>\n<p><strong>Policy 1130 Appointment, Assignment, Transfer and Promotion of Administrators</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 112.3135, F.S. 1001.32, F.S. 1012.22, F.S. 1012.23, F.S. 1012.2315, F.S. 1012.27, F.S. 1012.28, F.S. 1012.34, F.S. 1012.795, F.S. 1012.796<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policies 1211/ 3211/ 4211 Whistleblower Protection</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 112.3187<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 3120 Employment of Instructional Staff</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1012.01, F.S. 1012.22, F.S. 1012.24, F.S. 1012.27, F.S. 1012.315, F.S. 1012.32, F.S. 1012.33, F.S. 1012.42, F.S. 1012.55, F.S. 1012.56, F.S. 1012.57, F.S. 1012.575, F.A.C. 6A-1.0502, F.A.C. 6A-1.0503, 20 U.S.C. 6301, 20 U.S.C. 7801, F.A.C. 6A-4.002, 22 C.F.R. Part 62<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 3130 Appointment, Assignment, Transfer and Promotion of Instructional Staff</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 112.3135. F.S. 1001.32, F.S. 1004.04, F.S. 1012.22, F.S. 1012.23, F.S. 1012.2315, F.S. 1012.27, F.S. 1012.27, F.S. 1012.42, F.S. 1012.795, F.S. 1012.796, F.A.C. 6A-1.0503<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 3220 Evaluation of Instructional Personnel</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1012.01, F.S. 1012.22, F.S. 1012.28, F.S. 1012.31, F.S. 1012.34, F.A.C. 6A-5.030, F.A.C. 6A-5.0411<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 4120 Employment of Support Staff</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1001.10, F.S. 1012.01, F.S. 1012.315, F.S. 1012.37, F.S. 1012.40, F.S. 1012.56, F.A.C. 6A-1.0502(11), 20 U.S.C. 6301, 42 U.S.C. 9858f<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 4130 Assignments</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 112.3135, F.S. 1012.22, F.S. 1012.23, F.S. 1012.27, F.S. 1012.28, F.A.C. 6A-1.070<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 6520 Payroll Deductions</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1012.31, F.S. 447.303<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 7217 Weapons</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 790.001, F.S. 790.06, F.S. 790.115, F.S. 790.251, F.S. 1001.43(1)(a), F.S. 1006.07, 18 U.S.C. 922<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 7310 Disposition of Surplus Property</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 274.05, F.S. 274.06, F.S. 274.07, F.S. 1012.33, F.S. 1013.28, F.A.C. 69I-73.005, 2 C.F.R. 200.312, 2 C.F.R. 200.313<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8330 Student Records</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. Chapter 1119, F.S. 1001.41, F.S. 1001.52, F.S. 1002.22, F.S. 1002.221, F.S. 1002.222, F.S. 1003.25, F.A.C. 6A-1.0955, 20 U.S.C. Section 1232f through 1232i (FERPA), 20 U.S.C. 7908, 26 U.S.C. 152, 20 U.S.C. 1400 et seq., Individuals with Disabilities Act, Privacy Rights of Parents and Students - P.L. 90-247, 2021 Solomon Amendment: Subtitle C- General Service Authorities and Correction of Military Records SEC. 521<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8405 School Safety and Security</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1001.212, F.S. 1006.07, F.S. 1006.13, F.S. 1006.1493, Florida Safe Schools Assessment Tool, Threat Assessment in Schools: A Guide to Managing Threatening Situations and to Creating Safe School Climates (U.S. Secret Service and U.S. Department of Education), F.A.C. 6A-1.0018, F.A.C. 6AER23-02<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8407 Safe-School Officers</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 30.15, F.S. 1006.12, F.A.C. 6A-1.0018<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8470 Registered Sexual Predators/Sex Offenders</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 775.21, F.S. 775.25, F.S. 856.022, F.S. 943.0435, F.S. 944.606, F.S. 1006.695<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8475 Criminal Background Screening</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 435.12, F.S. 775.083, F.S. 1012.32, F.S. 1012.465, F.S. 1012.467, F.S. 1012.468, F.S. 775.082, F.S. 1012.56<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 9120 Public Communication and Parental Involvement Program</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 1002.45<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 9211 Direct-Support Organizations</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 11.45(8), F.S. 119.07(1), F.S. 1001.453, F.A.C. 6A-1.0013</p>\n<p><strong>Policy 9215 School-Support Organizations</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:<span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>Revisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span>F.S. 11.45(8), F.S. 119.07(1), F.S. 1001.41, F.S. 1001.42, F.S. 1001.43, F.S. 1001.453, F.S. 1010.01, F.S. 1010.20, F.S. 1011.07, F.A.C. 6A-1.001, F.A.C. 6A-1.0013, I.R.C. 170(f)(8), I.R.C. 170(f)(12), Title VI, Civil Rights Act of 1964, Title IX, Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504, Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Americans with Disabilities Act</p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl26_divTabs_1","title":"November 17, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County, Florida will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited for the purpose of conducting regular business.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose: November 17, 2026, 12:30 P.M. Work Session&nbsp;<br>\nNovember 17, 2026, 5:00 P.M. Board Meeting<br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;<span style=\"white-space: normal;\">Jim Miles Professional Development Center</span><br>\n4270 Wallace Road&nbsp;<br>\nLakeland, FL&nbsp; 33812-6344<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:&nbsp;If you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.&nbsp; If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:&nbsp;Notice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact the Superintendent’s Office of the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:&nbsp; October 28, 2026<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl26_divTabs_2","title":"November 3, 2026 - Notice of Election/Referendum","content":"<p>Notice is hereby given that a referendum election will be held throughout Polk County on November 3, 2026, at the polling place designated within each voting precinct of the County for the purpose of determining the following question:<br>\n<br>\nCounty School Board Referendum / Referéndum Junta Escolar del Condado<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Millage for School Safety, Teachers, and Career Education</strong></p>\n<p>Shall the Polk County School District levy an additional 1.0 mill in ad valorem taxes annually to fund school operations for teacher recruitment and retention and education support staff, for career and technical education, school safety, arts, and early learning--with proceeds shared with charter schools as required by law and monitored by an independent citizens' oversight committee?<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Tasa Impositiva para la Seguridad Escolar, los Maestros y la Educación Profesional</strong></p>\n<p>¿Debería el Distrito Escolar del Condado de Polk imponer anualmente una tasa adicional de 1.0 milésima en impuestos ad valorem para financiar las operaciones escolares destinadas a la contratación y retención de maestros y personal de apoyo educativo para la educación profesional y técnica, la seguridad escolar, las artes y la educación temprana,&nbsp;distribuyendo los fondos recaudados con las escuelas chárter según lo exige la ley y bajo la supervisión de un comité ciudadano independiente?<br>\n<br>\n_______ Yes / Sí<br>\n<br>\n_______ No / No<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<em>The polls will be open at the voting places on the date of such election from 7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.&nbsp; All qualified voters residing within Polk County may vote in said election.&nbsp; Early voting and absentee voting will be permitted upon compliance with the applicable provisions of general law.&nbsp;</em><br>\n<br>\n<span style=\"white-space: normal;\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>By:&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; Justin Sharpless, Board Chair</span><br>\n<span style=\"white-space: normal;\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t\t\t\t\t\t</span>Attest:&nbsp; Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</span><br>\n<br>\nPublication dates:&nbsp; September 28, 2026 and October 13, 2026</p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false}],// required,
						propPaneId: 'paneId', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propTitle: 'title', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propActive: 'active', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propDisabled: 'disabled', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propContent: 'content', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						tabMode: tabM,
						scrollToTabEdge: false, // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						disableScrollArrowsOnFullyScrolled: false // optional- pass in default value for demo purposes
					}).on('ready.scrtabs', function () {
						$('#' + this.id + ' .tab-pane').attr('tabindex', 0);
					});
				};

				activate();

            }
        }
	});

