				function activate() {
					$(tabObj).scrollingTabs({
						tabs: [{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_0","title":"April 28, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing","content":"<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0);\">NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public hearing or meeting to which all persons are invited.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose: April 28, 2026, to begin no earlier than 5:01 P.M.<br>\n<br>\nThe public hearing is for the following policy updates:<br>\n<br>\nBylaw 0147.1 TRAVEL AND EXPENSES<br>\nPolicy 5223 ABSENCES FOR RELIGIOUS INSTRUCTION<br>\n<br>\nLocation: School Board Auditorium, 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830<br>\n<br>\nAssistance: If you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice: Notice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact <strong>Chad Davis</strong>, Staff Attorney, Office of Superintendent of the School Board of Polk County, Florida P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:\tFebruary 25, 2026 <br>\n<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</span><br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_1","title":"April 22, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"Notice is hereby given that the School Board of Polk County, Florida will hold a public meeting or hearing for the purpose of conducting regular business.<br>\n<br>\nQuarterly Audit and Finance Committee Meeting<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Date/Time:</strong>\t\tApril 22, 2026 at 10:00 A.M.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Location:</strong>  \t\tFinance Conference Room - District Office<br>\n1915 South Floral Avenue Bartow, FL  33830<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Assistance:</strong>\tIf you require any type of accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at 863-534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Appeal Notice:</strong>\tNotice is given with accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing.  Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceedings at their own expense, usually with a court reporter.  The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.  <br>\n<br>\nPlease contact Carol Matthews, Senior Director of Audit Services, with any questions or if there is any additional information needed at <a href=\"mailto:carol.matthews@polk-fl.net\" class=\"ApplyClass\">carol.matthews@polk-fl.net</a><br>\n<br>\nDated:  April 8, 2026<br>\n<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_2","title":"April 14, 2026 & April 28, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA<br>\nNotice of Public Hearing or Meeting</strong></p>\n<p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County, Florida will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited for the purpose of conducting regular business.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose:\tApril 14, 2026, 9:00 A.M. Work Session <br>\nApril 28, 2026, 12:30 P.M. Work Session<br>\nApril 28, 2026, 5:00 P.M. Board Meeting<br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;School Board Auditorium, 1915 S. Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact the Superintendent’s Office of the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:  March 26, 2026<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_3","title":"April 14, 2026 - Notice Of Proposed Rule Development Workshop","content":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>NOTICE OF PROPOSED RULE DEVELOPMENT WORKSHOP<br>\nSCHOOL BOARD POLICY</strong></p>\n<p>The School Board of Polk County, Florida (“<strong>Board</strong>”) will hold a public workshop on the following revised Board policies <strong>Bylaw 0143.1, Bylaw 0169.1, Policy 1211, Policy 2261.02, Policy 2266, Policy 4241, Policy 2450, Policy 3120.04, Policy 3211, Policy 4120, Policy 4211, Policy 5330.01, Policy 5460, Policy 5780, Policy 8405, Policy 8420 and Policy 8470, on April 14, 2026</strong> at the Polk County Public Schools Administrative Offices, located at 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830. The proposed changes to the above referenced Board policies will be published on the Polk County Public Schools (“<strong>PCPS</strong>”) website as part of the meeting agenda seven days prior to the meeting. Meeting agendas can be accessed at:<br>\n<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/about/meetings\" title=\"Link to the Polk County Schools Meeting webpage\">https://www.polkschoolsfl.com/about/meetings</a><br>\n<br>\nThe proposed changes may be requested prior to the meeting agenda publication by emailing the Public Records Office at <a href=\"mailto:publicrecords@polkschoolsfl.incidentiq.com\" class=\"ApplyClass\">publicrecords@polkschoolsfl.incidentiq.com</a>. Copies may be obtained at the Polk County Public Schools Administrative Offices between the hours of 8:00 a.m. and 4:00 p.m. in the Public Records Office.<br>\n<br>\nThe revised Board policies will be placed on the Board’s agenda for a public hearing during the <strong>June 9, 2026</strong> meeting at the Polk County Public Schools Administrative Offices, located at 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830.<br>\n<br>\nWritten comments may be submitted within 21 days of the date of this notice to Legal Services, 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830. Substantially affected persons may, within 14 days of the date of this notice, file an objection to this rulemaking with the Board. The objection shall specify the portions of the proposed rules to which the person objects and the specific reasons for the objections. <br>\n<br>\n<strong>Bylaw 0143.1 Residence Areas</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions include modifications to various definitions.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language. <br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 1001.36, F.S. 1001.361, F.S. 1001.362<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Bylaw 0169.1 Public Participation at Board Meetings</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 286.011, F.S. 286.0114<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policies 1211/ 3211/ 4211 Whistleblower Protection</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:\tF.S. 112.3187, 112.3189</strong><br>\n<br>\n</p>\n<p><strong>Policy 2261.02 Title I – Parents’ Right to Know</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\t20 U.S.C. 6311, Elementary and Secondary Education Act of 1965, 34 C.F.R. Part 200 et seq.<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Policy 2266 Title IX Sexual Harassment Complaint and Investigation Procedures</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\t20 U.S.C. 1681 et seq., Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX), 20 U.S.C. 1400 et seq., The Individuals with Disabilities Education Improvement Act of 2004 (IDEIA), 42 U.S.C. 2000c et seq., Title IV of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, 42 U.S.C. 2000d et seq., 42 U.S.C. 2000e et seq., 42 U.S.C. 1983, 34 C.F.R. Part 106, Dear Colleague Letter on Sexual Violence (Office for Civil Rights, 2011), F.S. 1000.05, OCR’s Revised Sexual Harassment Guidance (2001)<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 2421 Career and Technical Education</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 445.004, F.S. 1003.4203, F.A.C. 6A-1.0014, F.A.C. 6A-10.0381, F.S. 445.006, F.S. 446 et seq., F.S. 450.081, F.S. 1000.05, F.S. 1001.42, F.S. 1003.01, F.S. 1003.41, F.S. 1003.4156, F.S. 1003.4282, F.S. 1003.491, F.S. 1003.492, F.S. 1003.493, F.S. 1003.4935, F.S. 1004.91, F.S. 1004.92, F.S. 1004.933, F.S. 1007.271, F.S. 1009.21, F.S. 1009.22, F.S. 1009.26, F.S. 1009.536, F.S. 1009.711, F.S. 1011.62, F.S. 1011.80, F.S. 1011.803, F.A.C. 6A-1.09442, F.A.C. 6A-6.0576, F.A.C. 6A-6.0200, F.A.C. 6A-10.0244, 29 U.SC. 201, 29 U.S.C. 202, 29 U.S.C. 203, 29 U.S.C. 204, 29 U.S.C. 206, 29 U.S.C. 207, 29 U.S.C. 209, 29 U.S.C. 210, 29 U.S.C. 211, 29 U.S.C. 212, 29 U.S.C. 213, 29 U.S.C. 214, 29 U.S.C. 215, 29 U.S.C. 216, 29 U.S.C. 216b, 29 U.S.C. 217, 29 U.S.C. 218, 29 U.S.C. 218b, 29 U.S.C. 218c, 29 U.S.C. 219<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Policy 2450 Adult and Community Education</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.A.C. 6A-1.0014, F.A.C. 6A-10.0381, F.S. 1003.435, F.S. 1004.93, F.S. 1004.94, The Veterans Benefits and Transition Act - 2018 (38 USC Sections 3679, 3698(c)(1)(C), P.L. 115-407, Sections 103-104)<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Policy 3120.04 Employment of Substitute, Limited Employment Agreement, <br>\nand Part-Time Instructional Staff</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 1012.35, 1012.36<br>\n<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 4120 Employment of Support Staff</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:\t</strong>Proposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 1001.10, F.S. 1012.01, F.S. 1012.315, F.S. 1012.37, F.S. 1012.40, F.S. 1012.56, F.A.C. 6A-1.0502(11), 20 U.S.C. 6301, 42 U.S.C. 9858f<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong style=\"font-size: 10pt;\">Policy 5330.01 Self-Administered Medication</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<strong><br>\nSummary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 985.04, F.S. 1002.20, F.S. 1002.221<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong style=\"font-size: 10pt;\">Policy 5460 Graduation Requirements</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\nSpecific Authority:\tF.S. 683.334, F.S. 683.335, F.S. 1002.3105, F.S. 1003.4281, F.S. 1003.4282, F.S. 1003.4285, F.S. 1003.4286, F.S. 1003.4295, F.S. 1003.433, F.S. 1003.435, F.S. 1003.436, F.S. 1003.437, F.S. 1003.453, F.A.C. 6A-1.0995, F.A.C. 6A-1.09961, F.A.C. 6A-1.09963, F.A.C. 6A-6.0573<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 5780 Student/Parent Rights</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 39.201, F.S. 381.0056, F.S. 394.463, F.S. 1000.05, F.S. 1002.20, F.S. 1002.22, F.S. 1002.385, F.S. 1002.39, F.S. 1002.394, F.S. 1002.395, F.S. 1002.40, F.S. 1002.41, F.S. 1002.411, F.S. 1002.43, F.S. 1003.01(13), F.S. 1003.02, F.S. 1003.21, F.S. 1003.22, F.S. 1003.3101, F.S. 1003.32, F.S. 1003.42, F.S. 1003.44, F.S. 1003.4505, F.S. 1003.47, F.S. 1003.52, F.S. 1003.53, F.S. 1003.55, F.S. 1003.56, F.S. <br>\n<br>\n1003.57, F.S. 1003.58, F.S. 1006.062(7), F.S. 1006.07, F.S. <br>\n1006.09, F.S. 1006.13, F.S. 1006.15, F.S. 1006.20, F.S. 1006.21, F.S. 1006.22, F.S. 1006.23, F.S. 1006.28, F.S. 1006.40, F.S. 1007.271, F.S. 1008.22, F.S. 1008.25, F.S. 1008.386, F.S. 1012.42, F.S. Chapter 1014, F.A.C. 6A-6.053, F.A.C. 6A-6.0533, F.S. 435.04(2), F.S. 1012.797<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8405 School Safety and Security</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 1001.212, F.S. 1006.07, F.S. 1006.13, F.S. 1006.1493, Florida Safe Schools Assessment Tool, Threat Assessment in Schools: A Guide to Managing Threatening Situations and to Creating Safe School Climates (U.S. Secret Service and U.S. Department of Education), F.A.C. 6A-1.0018, F.A.C. 6AER23-02<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Policy 8420 Emergency Management, Emergency Preparedness, and Emergency Response Agencies</strong><br>\n<br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tFlorida Fire Prevention Code (F.S. 633.202), F.S. 1001.43, F.S. 1006.07, F.S. 1006.07(6)(f), F.S. 1013.13, Fire Code (NFPA 1), Life Safety Code (NFPA 101)<br>\n<br>\n<strong></strong></p>\n<p><strong>Policy 8470 Registered Sexual Predators/ Sex Offender<br>\n</strong><br>\n<strong>Purpose and Effect:</strong>\tProposed revisions to comply with revised statutes and rules.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Summary:</strong>\tRevisions to existing language includes content, formatting, and terminology edits consistent with statutory language.<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Specific Authority:</strong>\tF.S. 775.21, F.S. 775.25, F.S. 856.022, F.S. 943.0435, F.S. 944.606, F.S. 1006.695<br>\n<br>\n</p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_4","title":"April 10, 2026 - Notice of Public Meeting or Hearing Special Meeting/Retreat","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN THAT THE SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA, announces a special meeting to which all persons are invited.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose:\tApril 10, 2026, 9:00 A.M. Special Meeting/Retreat<br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;Jim Miles Professional Development Center<br>\n4270 Wallace Road <br>\nLakeland, FL  33812-6344<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:\tIf you require any type of accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact the Superintendent’s Office of the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:  March 27, 2026<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl47_divTabs_5","title":"April 7, 2026 - Amended Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"<p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Attendance Boundary Committee Meeting</strong></p>\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong><strong>Date/Time:</strong> \tApril 7, 2026 at 5:30 P.M. <br>\n(Date corrected. This cancels the 3/3/26 previously noticed meeting.)<br>\n<br>\n<strong>Location:</strong> School Board District Office <br>\nFacilities &amp; Operations Conference Room <br>\nBuilding C<br>\n1909 South Floral Avenue <br>\nBartow, FL  33830 <br>\n<br>\n<strong>Assistance: </strong>\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771. <br>\n<br>\n<strong>Appeal Notice:</strong> \tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal. <br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this public meeting, please contact Facilities &amp; Operations for the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0620 ext. 886. <br>\n<br>\nDated: February 27, 2026<br>\n<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair <br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary </p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false}],// required,
