				function activate() {
					$(tabObj).scrollingTabs({
						tabs: [{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_0","title":"January 27, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing","content":"<p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public hearing or meeting to which all persons are invited.</p>\n<p>Date/Time/Purpose:  \tJanuary 27, 2026, to begin no earlier than 5:01 P.M.</p>\n<p>The public hearing is for the following policy updates:<br>\nPolicy 1120 EMPLOYMENT OF ADMINISTRATORS<br>\nPolicy 1121.01 BACKGROUND SCREENING AND EMPLOYMENT HISTORY CHECKS<br>\nPolicy 1129 CONFLICT OF INTEREST<br>\nPolicy 1139 EDUCATOR MISCONDUCT<br>\nPolicy 1210 STANDARDS OF ETHICAL CONDUCT<br>\nPolicy 1213 STUDENT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE<br>\nPolicy 1242 PROFESSIONAL LEARNING<br>\nPolicy 3120 EMPLOYMENT OF INSTRUCTIONAL STAFF<br>\nPolicy 3121.01 BACKGROUND SCREENING AND EMPLOYMENT HISTORY CHECKS<br>\nPolicy 3129 CONFLICT OF INTEREST<br>\nPolicy 3130 APPOINTMENT, ASSIGNMENT, TRANSFER, AND PROMOTION OF INSTRUCTIONAL STAFF<br>\nPolicy 3139 EDUCATOR MISCONDUCT<br>\nPolicy 3210 STANDARDS OF ETHICAL CONDUCT<br>\nPolicy 3213 STUDENT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE<br>\nPolicy 3242 PROFESSIONAL LEARNING<br>\nPolicy 3410 COMPENSATION<br>\nPolicy 3430.03 SICK LEAVE<br>\nPolicy 4120 EMPLOYMENT OF SUPPORT STAFF<br>\nPolicy 4121.01 BACKGROUND SCREENING AND EMPLOYMENT HISTORY CHECKS<br>\nPolicy 4129 CONFLICT OF INTEREST<br>\nPolicy 4210 STANDARDS OF ETHICAL CONDUCT<br>\nPolicy 4213 STUDENT SUPERVISION AND WELFARE<br>\nPolicy 4242 PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT<br>\nPolicy 1425 Nursing Mothers<br>\nPolicy 3425 Nursing Mothers<br>\nPolicy 4425 Nursing Mothers<br>\nPolicy 6144.01 Investments Purpose<br>\nPolicy 6325 Procurement - Federal Grants/Funs<br>\nPolicy 6550 Travel and Expenses<br>\nPolicy 7230 Gifts to the School District<br>\nPolicy 8280 Nursing Mothers<br>\n<br>\nLocation: School Board Auditorium, 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830</p>\n<p>Assistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.</p>\n<p>For further information about this meeting, please contact <strong>Chad Davis</strong>, Staff Attorney, Office of Superintendent of the School Board of Polk County, Florida P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.</p>\n<p>Dated:\tDecember 11, 2025 <br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</p>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_1","title":"January 27, 2026 -Notice of Special Meeting","content":"<p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County, Florida has scheduled a special meeting of the Finance Corporation to which all persons are invited.<br>\nDate/Time: \tJanuary 27, 2026 to begin no earlier than 5:01 P.M. <br>\n<br>\nPurpose: \tDiscuss and adopt Resolution No. 2025/2026-11<br>\n<br>\nA RESOLUTION OF THE SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA, APPROVING THE FORM OF AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF LEASE SCHEDULE NO. 2026 TO A MASTER LEASE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT RELATING TO THE LEASE-PURCHASE OF CERTAIN LAND, EQUIPMENT AND BUILDINGS CONSTITUTING EDUCATIONAL FACILITIES; APPROVING THE FORM AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF A SERIES 2026 SUPPLEMENTAL TRUST AGREEMENT PURSUANT TO WHICH THE TRUSTEE WILL EXECUTE, AUTHENTICATE AND DELIVER NOT TO EXCEED $305,000,000 IN AGGREGATE PRINCIPAL AMOUNT OF CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION, SERIES 2026 EVIDENCING FRACTIONAL UNDIVIDED INTERESTS OF THE OWNERS THEREOF IN BASIC RENT PAYMENTS TO BE MADE UNDER SUCH MASTER LEASE-PURCHASE AGREEMENT IN CONNECTION WITH THE FINANCING OF CERTAIN CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION; APPROVING U.S. BANK TRUST COMPANY, NATIONAL ASSOCIATION, AS SUCCESSOR TRUSTEE; AUTHORIZING THE CHAIR AND THE SUPERINTENDENT OF SCHOOLS TO AWARD THE SALE OF THE SERIES 2026 CERTIFICATES TO THE UNDERWRITERS WITHIN THE PARAMETERS SET FORTH HEREIN; APPROVING THE FORM OF AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF A CERTIFICATE PURCHASE CONTRACT RELATING TO THE NEGOTIATED SALE OF SUCH CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION UPON SUCH AWARD; APPROVING THE FORM OF A PRELIMINARY OFFERING STATEMENT AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF A FINAL OFFERING STATEMENT WITH RESPECT TO SUCH CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION; APPROVING THE FORM AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION AND DELIVERY OF A DISCLOSURE DISSEMINATION AGENT AGREEMENT; APPROVING THE FORM AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION OF A GROUND LEASE AGREEMENT; APPROVING THE FORM AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION OF A MEMORANDUM OF GROUND LEASE; AND APPROVING THE FORM AND AUTHORIZING THE EXECUTION OF AN ASSIGNMENT OF GROUND LEASE; DELEGATING AUTHORITY TO DETERMINE WHETHER TO UTILIZE MUNICIPAL BOND INSURANCE FOR ALL OR A PORTION OF SUCH CERTIFICATES; PROVIDING CERTAIN OTHER AUTHORIZATIONS AND DETAILS, AND PROVIDING AN EFFECTIVE DATE.<br>\n<br>\nLocation:\t\tSchool Board Auditorium, 1915 S. Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830</p>\n<p>Assistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.</p>\n<p>Appeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.</p>\n<p>For further information about this public meeting, please contact Heather Jenkins, Associate Superintendent Chief Financial Officers, School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831 at 863-457-4704. <br>\n<br>\nDated:\tDecember 10, 2025 <br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</p>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_2","title":"January 27, 2026 -Notice of Special Meeting ","content":"<p>NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County, Florida, has scheduled a special meeting of the Finance Corporation to which all persons are invited. <br>\n<br>\nDate/Time: \tJanuary 27, 2026 to begin no earlier than 5:01 P.M. <br>\n<br>\nPurpose: \tDiscuss and adopt Resolution No. 2025/2026-10<br>\n<br>\nTO APPROVE A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE CORPORATION TO ENTER INTO (I) A LEASE SCHEDULE NO. 2026, IN CONNECTION WITH THE ISSUANCE ON BEHALF OF THE SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA, OF NOT TO EXCEED $305,000,000 CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION (SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA, MASTER LEASE PROGRAM), SERIES 2026, FOR THE PURPOSE OF FINANCING ALL OR A PORTION OF CERTAIN EDUCATIONAL FACILITIES BEING LEASEPURCHASED BY THE SCHOOL BOARD, (II) A SERIES 2026 SUPPLEMENTAL TRUST AGREEMENT, (III) A CERTIFICATE PURCHASE CONTRACT, (IV) A GROUND LEASE AGREEMENT, (V) A MEMORANDUM OF GROUND LEASE, (VI) AN ASSIGNMENT OF GROUND LEASE AND RELATED DOCUMENTS; APPROVING THE DRAFTS OF THE OTHER RELATED FINANCING DOCUMENTS; APPROVING THE NEGOTIATED SALE OF THE CERTIFICATES TO THE UNDERWRITERS; AUTHORIZING THE PURCHASE OF A MUNICIPAL BOND INSURANCE POLICY; AND APPROVING OTHER MATTERS IN CONNECTION THEREWITH. <br>\n<br>\nLocation: \t\tSchool Board Auditorium, 1915 S. Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830</p>\n<p>Assistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.</p>\n<p>Appeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.</p>\n<p>For further information about this public meeting, please contact Heather Jenkins, Associate Superintendent Chief Financial Officers, School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-457-4704. <br>\n<br>\nDated:\tDecember 10, 2025 <br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary</p>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_3","title":"January 27, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing ","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public hearing or meeting to which all persons are invited.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose: January 27, 2026, to begin no earlier than 5:01 P.M.<br>\n<br>\nPublic hearing for the Student Progression Plan 2025 – 2026<br>\n<br>\nLocation: School Board Auditorium, 1915 South Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830<br>\n<br>\nAssistance: If you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact Ann Everett, Senior Director of Acceleration and Innovation, School Board of Polk County, Florida P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831 at 863-534-0631.<br>\n<br>\nDated:  December 12, 2025<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_4","title":"January 20, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited. <br>\n<br>\nAttendance Boundary Committee Meeting<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time: \tJanuary 20, 2026 at 5:30 P.M. <br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;School Board District Office <br>\nFacilities &amp; Operations Conference Room <br>\nBuilding C<br>\n1909 South Floral Avenue <br>\nBartow, FL  33830 <br>\n<br>\nAssistance: \tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771. <br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice: \tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal. <br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this public meeting, please contact Facilities &amp; Operations for the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0620 ext. 886. <br>\n<br>\n<br>\nDated: December 19, 2025<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair <br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary <br>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_5","title":"January 13, 2026 & January 27, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County, Florida will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited for the purpose of conducting regular business.<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose:\tJanuary 13, 2026, 9:00 A.M. Work Session <br>\nJanuary 27, 2026, 12:30 P.M. Work Session<br>\nJanuary 27, 2026, 5:00 P.M. Board Meeting<br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;School Board Auditorium, 1915 S. Floral Avenue, Bartow, FL 33830<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact the Superintendent’s Office of the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:  December 10, 2025<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_6","title":"January 13, 2026 - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that the School Board of Polk County will hold a public meeting or hearing to which all persons are invited. <br>\n<br>\nAttendance Boundary Committee Meeting<br>\n<br>\nDate/Time: \tJanuary 13, 2026 at 5:30 P.M. <br>\n<br>\nLocation: School Board District Office <br>\nFacilities &amp; Operations Conference Room <br>\nBuilding C<br>\n1909 South Floral Avenue <br>\nBartow, FL  33830 <br>\n<br>\nAssistance: \tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771. <br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice: \tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal. <br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this public meeting, please contact Facilities &amp; Operations for the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0620 ext. 886. <br>\n<br>\nDated: December 19, 2025<br>\n<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair <br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary <br>\n<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_7","title":"January 9, 2026 - Notice of Public Meeting or Hearing Special Meeting/Retreat ","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that THE SCHOOL BOARD OF POLK COUNTY, FLORIDA, announces a special meeting to which all persons are invited.  <br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose:\tJanuary 9, 2026, 9:00 A.M. Special Meeting/Retreat<br>\n<br>\nLocation:&nbsp;Jim Miles Professional Development Center<br>\n4270 Wallace Road <br>\nLakeland, FL  33812-6344<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:\tIf you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771.<br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:\tNotice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal.<br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this meeting, please contact the Superintendent’s Office of the School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-534-0521.<br>\n<br>\nDated:  December 10, 2025<br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>","active":false,"disabled":false},{"paneId":"ctl00_ContentPlaceHolder1_ctl56_divTabs_8","title":"January 8, 2026  - Notice of Public Hearing or Meeting ","content":"NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that members of the School Board of Polk County, Florida will participate in a panel discussion for Leadership Lakeland Class 42 to which all persons are invited. <br>\n<br>\nDate/Time/Purpose:  January 8, 2026 at 1:00 P.M. – 2:00 P.M.<br>\n<br>\nMore than one Polk County School Board member will be in attendance to participate in a discussion panel for the Leadership Lakeland Program. The purpose of the discussion panel is to better acquaint the class members with educational issues and topics within Polk County. Board members will introduce themselves, share why they decided to serve on the School Board and answer some prepared questions addressing community growth, efficient use of resources, preparing students for success, and how individuals and community organizations can support Polk County Public Schools. <br>\n<br>\nLocation:  Florida Southern College, 111 Lake Hollingsworth Drive, Lakeland, FL 33801<br>\n<br>\nAssistance:  If you require any type of an accommodation because of a disability to participate in the public meeting or hearing, please call the Office of Compliance and ADA at (863) 534-0513.  If you are deaf or hard of hearing, please contact us by calling the Florida Relay Service at 1-800-955-8771. <br>\n<br>\nAppeal Notice:  Notice is given in accordance with § 286.0105, Florida Statutes, that a record is required to appeal any decision the School Board makes at a public meeting or hearing. Those making an appeal need to preserve a verbatim record of the proceeding at their own expense, usually with a court reporter. The record must include the essential testimony and evidence required for any such appeal. <br>\n<br>\nFor further information about this public meeting, please contact Jeanette Crowley, Director of Strategic Partnerships, School Board of Polk County, Florida, P.O. Box 391, Bartow, Florida 33831, at 863-457-4708. <br>\n<br>\nDated:December 12, 2025 <br>\nBy: Justin Sharpless, Board Chair<br>\nAttest: Frederick R. Heid, Secretary<br>","active":false,"disabled":false}],// required,
						propPaneId: 'paneId', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propTitle: 'title', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
						propActive: 'active', // optional - pass in default value for demo purposes
